      "content": "that seems like a pretty tightrope to walk though. if we follow that \"harm prevention\" lead and start flagging satire because of the tropes it uses, aren't we basically just creating a way to censor any political commentary that's actually edgy or provocative? i've seen people argue that this approach just ends up silencing certain political viewpoints under the guise of safety. wouldn't that be a massive risk for a platform's growth and reputation?",
